{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-250826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If the sum of the first $32$ terms of an arithmetic series is ${S}_{32}=648,$ and the last term is ${a}_{32}=37.3,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the last term of our series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{N}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, ${a}_{N}$ is the last term, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting ${a}_{32}=37.3$, $N=32$, and ${S}_{N}=648$ into the formula above and solving for ${a}_{1}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}648 & =\\frac{32}{2}({a}_{1}+37.3) \\\\ 648 & =16({a}_{1}+37.3) \\\\ \\frac{648}{16} & ={a}_{1}+37.3 \\\\ 40.5 & ={a}_{1}+37.3 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =3.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e7666521bdb34d9aa2ce33fe700b4989434c1662087c40b7e3ddce51479f0c3"} {"question" "q-250826" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250826" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3.2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-233787" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If the sum of the first $50$ terms of an arithmetic series is ${S}_{50}=600,$ and the last term is ${a}_{50}=21.8,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-233787" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the last term of our series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{N}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, ${a}_{N}$ is the last term, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting ${a}_{50}=21.8$, $N=50$, and ${S}_{N}=600$ into the formula above and solving for ${a}_{1}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}600 & =\\frac{50}{2}({a}_{1}+21.8) \\\\ 600 & =25({a}_{1}+21.8) \\\\ \\frac{600}{25} & ={a}_{1}+21.8 \\\\ 24 & ={a}_{1}+21.8 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =2.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-233787" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e7666521bdb34d9aa2ce33fe700b4989434c1662087c40b7e3ddce51479f0c3"} {"question" "q-233787" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-233787" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2.2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If the sum of the first $20$ terms of an arithmetic series is ${S}_{20}=-635,$ and the last term is ${a}_{20}=-65,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the last term of our series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{N}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, ${a}_{N}$ is the last term, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting ${a}_{20}=-65$, $N=20$, and ${S}_{N}=-635$ into the formula above and solving for ${a}_{1}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-635 & =\\frac{20}{2}({a}_{1}+(-65)) \\\\ -635 & =10({a}_{1}-65) \\\\ -\\frac{635}{10} & ={a}_{1}-65 \\\\ -63.5 & ={a}_{1}-65 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250824" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e7666521bdb34d9aa2ce33fe700b4989434c1662087c40b7e3ddce51479f0c3"} {"question" "q-250824" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250824" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-108630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If the sum of the first $36$ terms of an arithmetic series is ${S}_{36}=\\frac{225}{2},$ and the last term is ${a}_{36}=\\frac{11}{2},$ what is the first term of the series?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-108630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the last term of our series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{N}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, ${a}_{N}$ is the last term, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting ${a}_{36}=\\frac{11}{2}$, $N=36$, and ${S}_{N}=\\frac{225}{2}$ into the formula above and solving for ${a}_{1}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{225}{2} & =\\frac{36}{2}({a}_{1}+\\frac{11}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{225}{36} & ={a}_{1}+\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ \\frac{25}{4} & ={a}_{1}+\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =\\frac{25}{4}-\\frac{11}{2} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-108630" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e7666521bdb34d9aa2ce33fe700b4989434c1662087c40b7e3ddce51479f0c3"} {"question" "q-108630" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-108630" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{11}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-108630" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-39255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If the sum of the first $18$ terms of an arithmetic series is ${S}_{18}=-495,$ and the last term is ${a}_{18}=-62,$ what is the first term of the series?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-39255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the last term of our series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}({a}_{1}+{a}_{N}),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, ${a}_{N}$ is the last term, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting ${a}_{18}=-62$, $N=18$, and ${S}_{N}=-495$ into the formula above and solving for ${a}_{1}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-495 & =\\frac{18}{2}({a}_{1}-62) \\\\ -495 & =9({a}_{1}-62) \\\\ \\frac{-495}{9} & ={a}_{1}-62 \\\\ -55 & ={a}_{1}-62 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-39255" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e7666521bdb34d9aa2ce33fe700b4989434c1662087c40b7e3ddce51479f0c3"} {"question" "q-39255" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-39255" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-39255" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-5606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the first term of an arithmetic series if the common difference is $d=-2,$ and the sum of the first $20$ terms is ${S}_{20}=-160?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-5606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=20$, $d=-2$, and ${S}_{N}=-160$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-160 & =\\frac{20}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(20-1)(-2)) \\\\ -160 & =10(2{a}_{1}-38) \\\\ -16 & =2{a}_{1}-38 \\\\ 22 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-5606" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e7666521bdb34d9aa2ce33fe700b4989434c1662087c40b7e3ddce51479f0c3"} {"question" "q-5606" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-5606" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "11"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "13"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-5606" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If the sum of the first $20$ terms of an arithmetic series is ${S}_{20}=301,$ and the common difference is $d=1.5,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=20$, $d=1.5$, and ${S}_{N}=301$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}301 & =\\frac{20}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(20-1)(1.5)) \\\\ 301 & =10(2{a}_{1}+28.5) \\\\ 30.1 & =2{a}_{1}+28.5 \\\\ 1.6 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250844" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e7666521bdb34d9aa2ce33fe700b4989434c1662087c40b7e3ddce51479f0c3"} {"question" "q-250844" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250844" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.8"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-233995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If the sum of the first $29$ terms of an arithmetic series is ${S}_{29}=319,$ and the common difference is $d=-3,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-233995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=29$, $d=-3$, and ${S}_{N}=319$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}319 & =\\frac{29}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(29-1)(-3)) \\\\ 638 & =29(2{a}_{1}-84) \\\\ 22 & =2{a}_{1}-84 \\\\ 106 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =53.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-233995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e7666521bdb34d9aa2ce33fe700b4989434c1662087c40b7e3ddce51479f0c3"} {"question" "q-233995" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-233995" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "53"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-5602" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the first term of an arithmetic series if the common difference is $d=-4,$ and the sum of the first $20$ terms is ${S}_{20}=1\\,160?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.j