/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250834" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-233997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If the $15$th term of an arithmetic series is $-53$ and the sum of the first $21$ terms is $-777,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-233997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=21$ and ${S}_{N}=-777$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ -777 & =\\frac{21}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(21-1)d) \\\\ -1\\,554= & 21(2{a}_{1}+20d) \\\\ -74 & =2{a}_{1}+20d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $15$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{15} & ={a}_{1}+(15-1)d \\\\ -53 & ={a}_{1}+14d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-53={a}_{1}+14d \\\\ -74=2{a}_{1}+20d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}106 & =-2{a}_{1}-28d \\\\ -74 & =2{a}_{1}+20d \\\\ 32 & =-8d \\\\ d & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=-4$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-53 & ={a}_{1}+14d \\\\ -53 & ={a}_{1}+14(-4) \\\\ -53 & ={a}_{1}-56 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-233997" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e7666521bdb34d9aa2ce33fe700b4989434c1662087c40b7e3ddce51479f0c3"} {"question" "q-233997" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-233997" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250881" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If the $6$th term of an arithmetic series is $\\frac{37}{4}$ and the sum of the first $16$ terms is $228,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250881" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=16$ and ${S}_{N}=228$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 228 & =\\frac{16}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(16-1)d) \\\\ 228 & =8(2{a}_{1}+15d) \\\\ \\frac{57}{2} & =2{a}_{1}+15d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $6$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{6} & ={a}_{1}+(6-1)d \\\\ \\frac{37}{4} & ={a}_{1}+5d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{37}{4}={a}_{1}+5d \\\\ \\frac{57}{2}=2{a}_{1}+15d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{37}{2} & =-2{a}_{1}-10d \\\\ \\frac{57}{2} & =2{a}_{1}+15d \\\\ \\frac{20}{2} & =5d \\\\ d & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=2$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{37}{4} & ={a}_{1}+5d \\\\ \\frac{37}{4} & ={a}_{1}+5(2) \\\\ \\frac{37}{4} & ={a}_{1}+\\frac{40}{4} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250881" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e7666521bdb34d9aa2ce33fe700b4989434c1662087c40b7e3ddce51479f0c3"} {"question" "q-250881" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250881" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{3}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250863" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If the $16$th term of an arithmetic series is $-32$ and the sum of the first $20$ terms is $-200,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250863" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=20$ and ${S}_{N}=-200$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ -200 & =\\frac{20}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(20-1)d) \\\\ -200 & =10(2{a}_{1}+19d) \\\\ -20 & =2{a}_{1}+19d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $16$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{16} & ={a}_{1}+(16-1)d \\\\ -32 & ={a}_{1}+15d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-32={a}_{1}+15d \\\\ -20=2{a}_{1}+19d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}64 & =-2{a}_{1}-30d \\\\ -20 & =2{a}_{1}+19d \\\\ 44 & =-11d \\\\ d & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=-4$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-32 & ={a}_{1}+15d \\\\ -32 & ={a}_{1}+15(-4) \\\\ -32 & ={a}_{1}-60 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =28.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250863" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e7666521bdb34d9aa2ce33fe700b4989434c1662087c40b7e3ddce51479f0c3"} {"question" "q-250863" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250863" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "28"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250878" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If the $9$th term of an arithmetic series is $\\frac{46}{3}$ and the sum of the first $15$ terms is $200,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250878" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=15$ and ${S}_{N}=200$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 200 & =\\frac{15}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(15-1)d) \\\\ 400 & =15(2{a}_{1}+14d) \\\\ \\frac{400}{15} & =2{a}_{1}+14d \\\\ \\frac{80}{3} & =2{a}_{1}+14d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $9$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{9} & ={a}_{1}+(9-1)d \\\\ \\frac{46}{3} & ={a}_{1}+8d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{46}{3}={a}_{1}+8d \\\\ \\frac{80}{3}=2{a}_{1}+14d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{92}{3} & =-2{a}_{1}-16d \\\\ \\frac{80}{3} & =2{a}_{1}+14d \\\\ -\\frac{12}{3} & =-2d \\\\ d & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=2$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{46}{3} & ={a}_{1}+8d \\\\ \\frac{46}{3} & ={a}_{1}+8(2) \\\\ \\frac{46}{3} & ={a}_{1}+16 \\\\ \\frac{46}{3} & ={a}_{1}+\\frac{48}{3} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250878" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e7666521bdb34d9aa2ce33fe700b4989434c1662087c40b7e3ddce51479f0c3"} {"question" "q-250878" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-250878" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{2}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-108724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the first term of an arithmetic series if its $5$th term is $-0.28$ and the sum of the first $12$ terms of the series is $-12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-108724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=12$ and ${S}_{N}=-12$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{12}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(12-1)d) \\\\ -12 & =6(2{a}_{1}+11d) \\\\ -2 & =2{a}_{1}+11d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $5$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{5} & ={a}_{1}+(5-1)d \\\\ -0.28 & ={a}_{1}+4d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-0.28={a}_{1}+4d \\\\ -2=2{a}_{1}+11d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.56 & =-2{a}_{1}-8d \\\\ -2 & =2{a}_{1}+11d \\\\ -1.44 & =3d \\\\ d & =-0.48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=-0.48$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-0.28 & ={a}_{1}+4(-0.48) \\\\ -0.28 & ={a}_{1}-1.92 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =1.64.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-108724" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8e7666521bdb34d9aa2ce33fe700b4989434c1662087c40b7e3ddce51479f0c3"} {"question" "q-108724" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-108724" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1.36"] ["math" "1.45"] ["math" "1.64"] ["math" "1.92"] ["math" "2.56"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "q-108724" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.64"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c9f7adce7c82bcf0301a91f4b08b8f06187d8c3742a79b6f4cdcc9df956781f"} {"question" "e-4206" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If the sum of the first $20$ terms of an arithmetic series is $S_{20}=560,$ and the last term is $a_{20}=66,$ what is the first term of the series?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/example-4206.json" "file_sha256" "8f0c60ba40fb6781b2a6f389497f410a5f34e3036a62346c19a209ef648218cb"} {"question" "e-4206" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the last term of our series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{N}{2}(a_1+a_N),\n$$\n\nwhere $a_1$ is the first term, $a_N$ is the last term, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $a_{20}=66,$ $N=20,$ and $S_N=560$ into the formula above and solving for $a_1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}560 & =\\frac{20}{2}({a}_{1}+66) \\\\ 560 & =10({a}_{1}+66) \\\\ \\frac{560}{10} & ={a}_{1}+66 \\\\ 56 & ={a}_{1}+66 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/example-4206.json" "file_sha256" "8f0c60ba40fb6781b2a6f389497f410a5f34e3036a62346c19a209ef648218cb"} {"question" "e-4207" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the first term of an arithmetic series if the common difference is $d=2,$ and the sum of the first $50$ terms is $S_{50}=2\\,150?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/example-4207.json" "file_sha256" "2e02d0999c4205636e3fe973ec9ede68a9afe0b3ead30942dcc6e1a76ec3ace8"} {"question" "e-4207" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{N}{2}\\big( 2a_1+(N-1)d \\big),\n$$\n\nwhere $a_1$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=50,$ $d=2,$ and $S_N=2\\,150$ into the formula above and solving for $a_1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\,150 & =\\frac{50}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(50-1)(2)) \\\\ 4\\,300 & =50(2{a}_{1}+98) \\\\ \\frac{4\\,300}{50} & =2{a}_{1}+98 \\\\ 86 & =2{a}_{1}+98 \\\\ -12 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/example-4207.json" "file_sha256" "2e02d0999c4205636e3fe973ec9ede68a9afe0b3ead30942dcc6e1a76ec3ace8"} {"question" "e-4208" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the first term of an arithmetic series if its $11$th term is $29$ and the sum of the first $16$ terms of the series is $384.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/example-4208.json" "file_sha256" "b0e657cf3c7b1e0c6dcc67832ebaa6ddae2b08146e475f26760128c3acbc7074"} {"question" "e-4208" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{N}{2}\\left( 2a_1+(N-1)d \\right),\n$$\n\nwhere $a_1$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N = 16$ and $S_N = 384$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 384 & =\\frac{16}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(16-1)d) \\\\ 384 & =8(2{a}_{1}+15d) \\\\ \\frac{384}{8} & =2{a}_{1}+15d \\\\ 48 & =2{a}_{1}+15d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $11$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{11} & ={a}_{1}+(11-1)d \\\\ 29 & ={a}_{1}+10d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}29={a}_{1}+10d \\\\ 48=2{a}_{1}+15d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-58 & =-2{a}_{1}-20d \\\\ 48 & =2{a}_{1}+15d \\\\ -10 & =-5d \\\\ d & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d = 2$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}29 & ={a}_{1}+10(2) \\\\ 29 & ={a}_{1}+20 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043304/example-4208.json" "file_sha256" "b0e657cf3c7b1e0c6dcc67832ebaa6ddae2b08146e475f26760128c3acbc7074"}] "usage" {"q-233997" [] "e-4208" [] "e-4207" [] "e-4206" [] "q-250844" [] "q-233787" [] "q-5602" []} "basis" 1604 "retractions" [[17592186078722 :question/problem "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nIf the sum of the first $50$ terms of an arithmetic series is $S_{50} = 600$, and the last term is $a_{50} = 21.8$, then the first term of the series is $a_{1} =$ {{field-1}}.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"finding-the-first-term-of-an-arithmetic-series-when-the-last-term-is-not-given\"></a>"] [17592186078751 :question/problem "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nIf the sum of the first $20$ terms of an arithmetic series is $S_{20} = 301$, and the common difference is $d = 1.5$, then the first term of the series is $a_{1} =$ {{field-1}}.\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"finding-the-first-term-of-an-arithmetic-series-given-a-term-and-the-sum\"></a>"] [17592186079043 :question/problem "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nWhat is the first term of an arithmetic series if the common difference is $d =-4$, and the sum of the first $20$ terms is $S_{20} = 1160$?"] [17592186078723 :question/problem "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nIf the $15$th term of an arithmetic series is $-53$ and the sum of the first $21$ terms is $-777$, then the first term of the series is $a_{1} =$ {{field-1}}."] [17592186078223 :question/problem "If the sum of the first $20$ terms of an arithmetic series is $S_{20}=560$, and the last term is $a_{20}=66$, what is the first term of the series?"] [17592186078223 :question/worked-solution "We are given the last term of our series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{N}{2}(a_1+a_N)\n$$\n\nwhere $a_1$ is the first term, $a_N$ is the last term, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $a_{20}=66$, $N=20$, and $S_N=560$ into the formula above and solving for $a_1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n560 &= \\frac{20}{2}(a_{1} + 66) \\\\\n560 &= 10(a_{1} + 66) \\\\\n\\frac{560}{10} &= a_{1} + 66 \\\\\n56 &= a_{1} + 66 \\\\\na_{1} &= -10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186078224 :question/problem "What is the first term of an arithmetic series if the common difference is $d=2$, and the sum of the first $50$ terms is $S_{50}=2\\,150$?"] [17592186078224 :question/worked-solution "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{N}{2}\\big(2a_1+(N-1)d \\big)\n$$\n\nwhere $a_1$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=50$, $d=2$, and $S_N=2\\,150$ into the formula above and solving for $a_1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2150 &= \\frac{50}{2}(2a_{1} + (50 - 1)(2)) \\\\\n4300 &= 50(2a_{1} + 98) \\\\\n\\frac{4300}{50} &= 2a_{1} + 98 \\\\\n86 &= 2a_{1} + 98 \\\\\n- 12 &= 2a_{1} \\\\\na_{1} &= -6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186078225 :question/problem "Find the first term of an arithmetic series if its $11$th term is $29$ and the sum of the first $16$ terms of the series is $384$."] [17592186078225 :question/worked-solution "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{N}{2}\\left(2a_1+(N-1)d \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere $a_1$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N = 16$ and $S_N = 384$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nS_{N} &= \\frac{N}{2}(2a_{1} + (N - 1)d) \\\\\n384 &= \\frac{16}{2}(2a_{1} + (16 - 1)d) \\\\\n384 &= 8(2a_{1} + 15d) \\\\\n\\frac{384}{8} &= 2a_{1} + 15d \\\\\n48 &= 2a_{1} + 15d\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $11$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na_{n} &= a_{1} + (n - 1)d \\\\\na_{11} &= a_{1} + (11 - 1)d \\\\\n29 &= a_{1} + 10d\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{29 = a_{1} + 10d; 48 = 2a_{1} + 15d\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-58 &= -2a_{1} - 20d \\\\\n48 &= 2a_{1} + 15d \\\\\n- 10 &= -5d \\\\\nd &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d = 2$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n29 &= a_{1} + 10(2) \\\\\n29 &= a_{1} + 20 \\\\\na_{1} &= 9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186077470 17592186077471 17592186077472 17592186077473 17592186077474 17592186232843 17592186232844 17592186232866] "immutable_fields" [[17592186075693 :answer-field/correct] [17592186075693 :answer-field/id] [17592186075693 :answer-field/key] [17592186075693 :answer-field/type] [17592186075694 :answer-field/correct] [17592186075694 :answer-field/id] [17592186075694 :answer-field/key] [17592186075694 :answer-field/type] [17592186075762 :answer-field/correct] [17592186075762 :answer-field/id] [17592186075762 :answer-field/key] [17592186075762 :answer-field/type] [17592186077469 :answer-field/correct] [17592186077469 :answer-field/id] [17592186077469 :answer-field/key] [17592186077469 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
